# What the build context is allowed to carry.
#
# The COPY lines in the Dockerfile are selective, so none of this would reach
# the image anyway. It is excluded because the **context** is sent to the
# daemon and cached, and `data/` is somebody's actual ledger and `secret.key`.
# A build context is not a place to put those, even in transit.
.git
.github
data
backups
ci-data
e2e-data
.venv
client/node_modules
client/dist
app/static/dist
**/__pycache__
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.temp
**/.DS_Store

# The client is built inside the image, from source. Shipping a local build in
# would mean the image's UI depends on whatever was last on somebody's laptop.
